# libcksum89

Four fixed checksum algorithms with streaming and one-shot interfaces, in
strict ISO C89.

```text
CRC-32/ISO-HDLC   CRC-32C   CRC-64/NVME   INET16 (RFC 1071)
```

## Boundaries

| Concern | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| checksum mathematics | `libcksum89` |
| streaming state | caller (public context value) |
| allocation, I/O, dispatch | nobody; the library has none |
| wire byte order, framing, checksum field placement | protocol or format layer |
| error reporting | nobody; operations are total under pointer preconditions |

`libcksum89` calculates values. Callers encode them.

## Build and test

- `just build` - build `build/libcksum89.a`.
- `just smoke` - one end-to-end path through all four algorithms.
- `just unit` - vectors, differential corpora, streaming algebra, context
  laws, alignment, and lookup-table integrity.
- `just guard` - the `CHAR_BIT == 8` compile-time rejection probe.
- `just cpp-check` - C++23 header inclusion with g++ and clang++.
- `just test` - all fast suites.
- `just audit` - symbol/API audit: no allocation or I/O references and an
  exact export set.
- `just sanitize` - ASan + UBSan rebuild and full suite.
- `just matrix` - gcc/clang x C89/C23 build-and-run matrix.
- `just tables` - regenerate the checked-in lookup tables.
- `just check` - green profile, lint, and all fast suites.

## Conventions

- Public API namespaced `cksum89_*`, declared in `include/cksum89.h`.
- Contexts are caller-owned value types; `final` does not mutate.
- Test-driven: scenario -> acceptance -> failing test -> minimal code ->
  refactor.
- `main` stays green; no pushes without permission.

See `spec/cksum89-spec.md` for the normative contract and `.agent/` for the
concept, design, scenarios, and acceptance criteria.
